{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI17EnvironmentValuesV7refreshAA13RefreshActionVSgvp","title":"refresh","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refresh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"set","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When this environment value contains an instance of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction"},{"type":"text","text":" structure, certain built-in views in the corresponding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment"},{"type":"text","text":" begin offering a refresh capability. They apply the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance’s handler to any refresh operation that the user initiates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"By default, the environment value is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":", but you can use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View\/refreshable(action:)"},{"type":"text","text":" modifier to create and store a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refresh action that uses the handler that you specify:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["List(mailbox.conversations) { conversation in","    ConversationCell(conversation)","}",".refreshable {","    await mailbox.fetch()","}"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On iOS and iPadOS, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"List"},{"type":"text","text":" in the example above offers a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pull to refresh gesture because it detects the refresh action. When"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the user drags the list down and releases, the list calls the action’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler. Because OpenSwiftUI declares the handler as asynchronous, it can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safely make long-running asynchronous calls, like fetching network data."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Refreshing Custom Views","anchor":"Refreshing-Custom-Views","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also offer refresh capability in your custom views."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Read the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":" environment value to get the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance for a given "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment"},{"type":"text","text":". If you find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" value, change your view’s appearance or behavior to offer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the refresh to the user, and call the instance to conduct the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refresh. You can call the refresh instance directly because it defines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()"},{"type":"text","text":" method that Swift calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when you call the instance:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct RefreshableView: View {","    @Environment(\\.refresh) private var refresh","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Refresh\") {","            Task {","                await refresh?()","            }","        }","        .disabled(refresh == nil)","    }","}"],"syntax":null},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Be sure to call the handler asynchronously by preceding it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":". Because the call is asynchronous, you can use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its lifetime to indicate progress to the user. For example,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can reveal an indeterminate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProgressView"},{"type":"text","text":" before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calling the handler, and hide it when the handler completes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your code isn’t already in an asynchronous context, create a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/Task"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method to run in. If you do this, consider adding a way for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"user to cancel the task. For more information, see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"The Swift Programming Language","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues/refresh":{"title":"refresh","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refresh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RefreshAction","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RefreshAction"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RefreshAction"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An action that initiates a refresh operation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction","title":"RefreshAction","kind":"symbol"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction/callAsFunction()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initiates a refresh action."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction\/callasfunction()","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()","title":"callAsFunction()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"callAsFunction"},{"kind":"text","text":"() "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"async"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"title":"OpenSwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","abstract":[]},"https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/LanguageGuide/Concurrency.html":{"title":"Concurrency","url":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Concurrency"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnvironmentValues"}],"title":"EnvironmentValues","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnvironmentValues"}],"abstract":[{"text":"OpenSwiftUI exposes a collection of values to your app’s views in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"EnvironmentValues","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" structure. To read a value from the structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declare a property using the ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","isActive":true},{"text":" property wrapper and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specify the value’s key path. For example, you can read the current locale:","type":"text"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Environment":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Environment"}],"title":"Environment","role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environment","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Environment","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A property wrapper that reads a value from a view’s environment."}]}}}